<title>FRANCE: Goldman Sachs raises rating on Elf.</title>
<headline>Goldman Sachs raises rating on Elf.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage Goldman Sachs has raised the rating on the stock of French oil company Elf Aquitaine to market outperformer from market performer.</p>
<p>The brokerage confirmed the upgrade, reported by market sources, but the analyst was not available to discuss the reasons.</p>
<p>Shares in Elf were up 1.76 percent at 519 francs at 1540 GMT. Shares in rival Total were up 0.74 percent at 450.30 francs in a declining market. Traders said both shares were also helped by the dollar's strong gains.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
